  SECURITY REPORT — Score: 78/100 [MEDIUM]
  The codebase has a few notable security concerns: a publicly exposed seed endpoint, hard‑coded passwords, overly permissive CORS, missing maximum length validation on user‑supplied strings, and no rate limiting on auth routes. Addressing these issues will significantly improve the overall security posture.

  Findings (5):
  [HIGH    ] AuthenticationGap in app/routes/seed_routes.py
             The seed endpoint is publicly accessible without any authentication, allowing anyone to create users, posts, and tags.
             Fix: Protect the route with an authentication dependency (e.g., Depends(get_current_user) or a dedicated admin check) and restrict it to authorized personnel only.
  [MEDIUM  ] HardcodedSecret in app/routes/seed_routes.py
             Plain‑text passwords are hard‑coded in the source for seed users, exposing credentials if the repository is leaked.
             Fix: Remove hard‑coded passwords. Store seed credentials in environment variables or generate them at runtime, and only store the hashed version in the database.
  [MEDIUM  ] CORSIssue in app/main.py
             CORS is configured to allow any origin, which is unsafe for a production deployment and can expose the API to malicious front‑ends.
             Fix: Replace the wildcard with a whitelist of trusted origins, e.g., allow_origins=["https://myfrontend.com"] and set allow_credentials accordingly.
  [MEDIUM  ] MissingValidation in app/schemas/post.py
             String fields are only constrained by a minimum length; there is no maximum length, allowing excessively large payloads that could lead to DoS or other issues.
             Fix: Add appropriate max_length constraints, e.g., Field(min_length=1, max_length=255) for titles, emails, display names, etc.
  [LOW     ] AuthenticationGap in app/routes/auth_routes.py
             Authentication endpoints lack any rate‑limiting, making them vulnerable to credential‑stuffing and brute‑force attacks.
             Fix: Integrate a rate‑limiting middleware such as SlowAPI or implement custom throttling to limit requests per IP address.

  Passed: No SQL injection found, Passwords properly hashed with bcrypt
